+
+/**
+ * Hearth: what became of the foreground service the location task asked for.
+ * Android 12 refuses a start from the background except at a few moments
+ * (a geofence exit, an activity transition, a high priority push, an app
+ * exempt from battery optimisation among them), and the refusal used to be
+ * either thrown before the request was registered or invisible to JS. The
+ * consumer records the outcome here and the module hands it to JS, so the app
+ * can keep its fence armed and try again at the next allowed moment.
+ *
+ * "none": no service wanted or it has been stopped. "starting": the start was
+ * accepted and the bind is in flight. "running": in the foreground with its
+ * notification. "refused": Android did not allow the start.
+ */
+object ForegroundServiceState {
+  @Volatile var status = "none"
+}
